That have been far too few HP's to ascend in my last game...

After I have got The Book from the Wizard, I just had HP:123, and it
was no problem at all. But then, down at the Sanctum, but especially
at the Elemental Planes (mostly Air, with the all elementals), I had
to quaff really lot of full healing to survive (that finally put me
up to HP:218). More than once I had quickly been hit down to around
40 HP's. That continued at the Astral level where, faster than I was
aware, was down at 40 HP's more than once, even if I already was
around maxHP:200 at that time; cannot say how that could happen.

My equipment was somewhat non-standard for me; a BDSM (did not find
any grey dragon on my way down), a bulky shield of reflection, and,
since I had a helmet of telepathy, I used that AoLS, instead of ESP.
Despite some polypile sessions I did not get any ring of levitation
so I had to change my speed boots for levitation boots on Air.

Water level was tedious; I had no means to confuse myself[*] to find
the portal, but tons of gold detection scrolls (which I was usually
lacking). So accidentally stepped into the water and fortunately got
only some unimportant scrolls blanked. Using The Amulet that got hot
very often I finally found the portal beneath some corpse. :-/

[*] Thought I might either find some potion or some spell would have
been forgotten until then. In retrospect, I should not have used the
booze on Earth level.

Wanted to go two-weaponing, then, (+6 Excalibur and +6 silver saber)
so put away the shield of reflection (and forgot to put on the amulet
of reflection, that I think found later in the game; Sokoban provided
the bag, IIRC). Finally, near the second altar, I noticed that I am
missing some ring and the charged wand of death in my main inventory.
(As far as I know, zapping a wand of death at yourself will kill you.
Not sure what happens if you break that wand, or if it explodes due
to some lightning/shock blast.) Must have been some effective shock
attack against my Knight.

Also on Astral I was very often hit down to HP:40; I was frightened
by that. But thanks to the colored-HP's patch (thanks again for that
great feature! :-)  I always noticed it in time and could quaff the
full healing.

Ah, and the endgame log mentioned that I used one wish; wishing for
two (and got one) blessed scrolls of charging from the castle's wand
of wishing (0:1)! :-o

